IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ppl-logic`
IMPORT `ppl-time`
IMPORT `ppl-nouns`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425, Chapter 2 Part 2-3 Division 2 (sections 31AA to 31A): eligibility on a flexible PPL day.
-- The Australian residency test, caring, the work test and the income test are other Divisions (or are outside the sources) and arrive here as facts about the claimant on the day.
-- A fact that depends on the PPL rules (what counts as exceptional circumstances, the prescribed conditions) is asked as a fact.

GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the claimant satisfies the work test and the income test if they have not previously satisfied both` MEANS
    IF f's `has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child`
    THEN `both results hold` (f's `satisfies the work test on the day`) (f's `satisfies the income test on the day`)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the claimant meets the birth-day conditions` MEANS
    JUST (        (f's `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born`)
          AND (   (NOT (f's `the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period the person is subject to`))
               OR (f's `subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the person on the day the child was born`)))

-- src:578 | (2) A person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child if:
-- src:579 | (a) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on that day; and
-- src:580 | (b) the person is caring for the child on that day; and
-- src:581 | (c) on that day the person is performing no more than one hour of paid work; and
-- src:582 | (d) if the person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child—the person satisfies the work test and the income test on that day; and
-- src:583 | (e) both of the following apply:
-- src:584 | (i) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born;
-- src:585 | (ii) if the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident’s waiting period that the person is subject to under section 31A—subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the person on the day the child was born.
@ref s 31AA(2) (src:578-585)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is eligible under the main eligibility rule` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds`
        (LIST JUST (f's `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day`)
            , JUST (f's `is caring for the child on the day`)
            , JUST (`the hours of paid work on the day are no more than one` (f's `hours of paid work performed on the day`))
            , `the claimant satisfies the work test and the income test if they have not previously satisfied both` f
            , `the claimant meets the birth-day conditions` f)

-- src:587 | (3) A person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child if:
-- src:588 | (a) the child is stillborn or has died before that day; and
-- src:589 | (b) on that day, the person would be eligible under subsection (2) for parental leave pay on that day, if paragraphs (2)(b) and (c) were disregarded; and
-- src:590 | (c) the person would have been caring for the child on that day had the child not been stillborn or died.
@ref s 31AA(3) (src:587-590)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is eligible when the child is stillborn or has died` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds`
        (LIST JUST (f's `the child is stillborn or has died before the day`)
            , JUST (f's `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day`)
            , `the claimant satisfies the work test and the income test if they have not previously satisfied both` f
            , `the claimant meets the birth-day conditions` f
            , JUST (f's `would have been caring for the child on the day had the child not been stillborn or died`))

-- src:592 | (4) A person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child if:
-- src:593 | (a) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on that day; and
-- src:594 | (b) if the person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child—the person satisfies the work test and the income test on that day; and
-- src:595 | (c) both of the following apply:
-- src:596 | (i) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born;
-- src:597 | (ii) if the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident’s waiting period that the person is subject to under section 31A—subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the person on the day the child was born; and
-- src:598 | (d) the person does not satisfy the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a special PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:599 | (e) on that flexible PPL day, the person satisfies the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 31AA(4) (src:592-599)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is eligible when they meet prescribed conditions and are not a special PPL claimant in exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds`
        (LIST JUST (f's `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day`)
            , `the claimant satisfies the work test and the income test if they have not previously satisfied both` f
            , `the claimant meets the birth-day conditions` f
            , JUST (NOT (f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a special PPL claim can be made`))
            , JUST (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AA(4)(e)`))

-- src:601 | (5) A person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child if:
-- src:602 | (a) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on that day; and
-- src:603 | (b) both of the following apply:
-- src:604 | (i) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born;
-- src:605 | (ii) if the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident’s waiting period that the person is subject to under section 31A—subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the person on the day the child was born; and
-- src:606 | (c) the person satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a special PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:607 | (d) on that flexible PPL day, the person satisfies the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 31AA(5) (src:601-607)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is eligible when they meet prescribed conditions and are a special PPL claimant in exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds`
        (LIST JUST (f's `satisfies the Australian residency test on the day`)
            , `the claimant meets the birth-day conditions` f
            , JUST (f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a special PPL claim can be made`)
            , JUST (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AA(5)(d)`))

-- src:612 | (2) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if:
-- src:613 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:614 | (b) neither the relevant claimant nor the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made.
@ref s 31AB(2) (src:612-614)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(2) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        `determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` (f's `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force for any person`) (`the total limit of flexible PPL days for a child born on` born)
          AND (NOT ((f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`) OR (f's `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`))))

-- src:616 | (3) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if:
-- src:617 | (a) the relevant claimant has a partner at the time the relevant claimant makes their first effective claim in relation to the child; and
-- src:618 | (b) one or more determinations under section 13 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(2); and
-- src:619 | (c) neither the relevant claimant nor the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:620 | (d) the relevant claimant does not satisfy the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 31AB(3) (src:616-620)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(3) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        (f's `has a partner at the time of making the first effective claim in relation to the child`)
          AND `determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` (f's `flexible PPL days covered by determinations under section 13 in force for the claimant`) (`the claimant limit of flexible PPL days when partnered, for a child born on` born)
          AND (NOT ((f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`) OR (f's `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`)))
          AND (NOT (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(3)(d)`)))

-- src:622 | (4) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if:
-- src:623 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:624 | (b) the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:625 | (c) the relevant claimant does not satisfy the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of paragraph (5)(c).
@ref s 31AB(4) (src:622-625)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(4) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        `determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` (f's `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force for the claimant or the claimant's partner`) (`the total limit of flexible PPL days for a child born on` born)
          AND ((f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`) OR (f's `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`))
          AND (NOT (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(5)(c)`)))

-- src:627 | (5) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if:
-- src:628 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:629 | (b) the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:630 | (c) the relevant claimant satisfies the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 31AB(5) (src:627-630)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(5) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        `determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` (f's `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force for the claimant or the claimant's partner`) (`the total limit of flexible PPL days for a child born on` born)
          AND ((f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`) OR (f's `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`))
          AND (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(5)(c)`))

-- src:632 | (6) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if:
-- src:633 | (a) the relevant claimant has a partner at the time the relevant claimant makes their first effective claim in relation to the child; and
-- src:634 | (b) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(2); and
-- src:635 | (c) the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:636 | (d) the relevant claimant satisfies the conditions prescribed by the PPL rules for the purposes of paragraph (5)(c).
@ref s 31AB(6) (src:632-636)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(6) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (        (f's `has a partner at the time of making the first effective claim in relation to the child`)
          AND `determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` (f's `flexible PPL days covered by determinations under section 13 or 14 in force for the claimant`) (`the claimant limit of flexible PPL days when partnered, for a child born on` born)
          AND ((f's `satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`) OR (f's `the claimant's partner satisfies the circumstances prescribed as exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`))
          AND (f's `satisfies the conditions prescribed for paragraph 31AB(5)(c)`))

-- src:638 | (7) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if the relevant claimant is deceased on that day.
@ref s 31AB(7) (src:638-638)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(7) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST (f's `the claimant is deceased on the day`)

-- src:640 | (8) This subsection applies to the relevant claimant on a flexible PPL day if that day is in a newly arrived resident’s waiting period for the relevant claimant (see section 31A).
-- src:706 | (7) Subsection 31AB(8) does not apply to a person in respect of a day in the newly arrived resident’s waiting period for the person if on that day the person holds, or is the former holder of, a visa in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of subsection 739A(6) of the Social Security Act.
-- src:707 | (7A) Subsection 31AB(8) does not apply to a person in respect of a day (the assessment day) in the newly arrived resident’s waiting period for the person if:
-- src:708 | (a) on the assessment day the person is a refugee or a former refugee; or
-- src:709 | (b) the following apply:
-- src:710 | (i) the person was a family member of another person at the time the other person became a refugee before the assessment day;
-- src:711 | (ii) the person is a family member of that other person on the assessment day or, if that other person has died, the person was a family member of that other person immediately before that other person died; or
-- src:712 | (c) the person is an Australian citizen on the assessment day; or
-- src:713 | (d) the person is residing in Australia on the assessment day and has held a special category visa on any day before the assessment day.
@ref s 31AB(8), with the exceptions in s 31A(7) and (7A) (src:640-713)
GIVEN f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(8) applies to the relevant claimant` MEANS
    JUST ((f's `the day is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period for the claimant`) AND (NOT (f's `subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies to the claimant on the day`)))

-- src:610 | (1) A person (the relevant claimant) is not eligible for parental leave pay on a day that is a flexible PPL day for a child if subsection (2), (3), (4), (5), (6), (7) or (8) applies to the relevant claimant on that day.
@ref s 31AB(1) (src:610-610)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is not eligible on a flexible PPL day under section 31AB` MEANS
    `some result in a list holds`
        (LIST `subsection 31AB(2) applies to the relevant claimant` born f
            , `subsection 31AB(3) applies to the relevant claimant` born f
            , `subsection 31AB(4) applies to the relevant claimant` born f
            , `subsection 31AB(5) applies to the relevant claimant` born f
            , `subsection 31AB(6) applies to the relevant claimant` born f
            , `subsection 31AB(7) applies to the relevant claimant` f
            , `subsection 31AB(8) applies to the relevant claimant` f)

-- src:574 | (1) A person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child if:
-- src:575 | (a) the person is eligible for parental leave pay on the day under subsection (2), (3), (4) or (5); and
-- src:576 | (b) the person is not ineligible for parental leave pay on the day under section 31AB.
@ref s 31AA(1) (src:574-576)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, f IS A `The claimant's facts on a flexible PPL day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is eligible for parental leave pay on a flexible PPL day for a child` MEANS
    `both results hold`
        (`some result in a list holds`
            (LIST `a person is eligible under the main eligibility rule` f
                , `a person is eligible when the child is stillborn or has died` f
                , `a person is eligible when they meet prescribed conditions and are not a special PPL claimant in exceptional circumstances` f
                , `a person is eligible when they meet prescribed conditions and are a special PPL claimant in exceptional circumstances` f))
        (`the opposite of a result` (`a person is not eligible on a flexible PPL day under section 31AB` born f))

-- src:658 | (1) Subject to this section, a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period if, on or after the commencement of this subsection, the person:
-- src:659 | (a) becomes the holder of a visa determined by the Minister for the purposes of subparagraph 729(2)(f)(v) of the Social Security Act; or
-- src:660 | (b) becomes the holder of a permanent visa, except:
-- src:661 | (i) a visa referred to in the regulations under the Migration Act 1958 as a Subclass 117 (Orphan Relative) visa or as a Subclass 837 (Orphan Relative) visa; or
-- src:662 | (ii) a visa referred to in the regulations under the Migration Act 1958 as a Subclass 115 (Remaining Relative) visa or as a Subclass 835 (Remaining Relative) visa; or
-- src:663 | (iii) a visa of a kind determined in an instrument under subsection (1A).
-- src:664 | (1A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine a kind of visa for the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(iii).
-- src:665 | (1B) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply in relation to a person if, at any time before the commencement of this subsection, the person held a visa covered by paragraph (1)(a).
@ref s 31A(1)-(1B) (src:658-665)
GIVEN `the person became the holder of a visa on or after the commencement of subsection 31A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the visa is one determined by the Minister for the purposes of subparagraph 729(2)(f)(v) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the visa is a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permanent visa is one of the kinds that subparagraphs 31A(1)(b)(i) to (iii) except` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at any time before the commencement of subsection 31A(1B) the person held a visa covered by paragraph 31A(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person is subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period under subsection 31A(1)` MEANS
    JUST (        `the person became the holder of a visa on or after the commencement of subsection 31A(1)`
          AND (   `the visa is one determined by the Minister for the purposes of subparagraph 729(2)(f)(v) of the Social Security Act`
               OR (        `the visa is a permanent visa`
                   AND (NOT `the permanent visa is one of the kinds that subparagraphs 31A(1)(b)(i) to (iii) except`)
                   AND (NOT `at any time before the commencement of subsection 31A(1B) the person held a visa covered by paragraph 31A(1)(a)`))))

-- src:667 | (2) If:
-- src:668 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:669 | (b) the visa covered by paragraph (1)(a) or (b) is in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(3)(b) of the Social Security Act; and
-- src:670 | (c) subsection (3) does not apply;
-- src:671 | the waiting period:
-- src:672 | (d) starts on the day on which the person applied for that visa; and
-- src:673 | (e) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:674 | (3) If:
-- src:675 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:676 | (b) the person has previously held one or more visas in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(4)(b) of the Social Security Act;
-- src:677 | the waiting period:
-- src:678 | (c) starts on the day on which the person applied for the last of those visas; and
-- src:679 | (d) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:680 | (4) If:
-- src:681 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:682 | (b) neither subsection (2) nor (3) applies to the person;
-- src:683 | the waiting period starts on the day on which the person:
-- src:684 | (c) first entered Australia; or
-- src:685 | (d) becomes the holder of a permanent visa;
-- src:686 | whichever occurs last, and ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
@ref s 31A(2)-(4) (src:667-686)
GIVEN `the person is subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the visa is in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(3)(b) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has previously held one or more visas in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(4)(b) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person applied for that visa` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person applied for the last of those visas` IS A DATE
      `the day the person first entered Australia` IS A DATE
      `the day the person became the holder of a permanent visa` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day a newly arrived resident's waiting period starts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the person is subject to a newly arrived resident's waiting period` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the person has previously held one or more visas in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(4)(b) of the Social Security Act`
           THEN JUST `the day on which the person applied for the last of those visas`
           IF `the visa is in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(3)(b) of the Social Security Act`
           THEN JUST `the day on which the person applied for that visa`
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the day a newly arrived resident's waiting period starts under subsection (4)` `the day the person first entered Australia` `the day the person became the holder of a permanent visa`)

-- src:688 | (6A) If:
-- src:689 | (a) a person has made an effective claim for parental leave pay for a flexible PPL day for a child; and
-- src:690 | (b) the person was receiving any of the following on the day before that flexible PPL day:
-- src:691 | (i) a social security pension;
-- src:692 | (ii) a social security benefit;
-- src:693 | (iii) farm household allowance;
-- src:694 | (iv) parental leave pay for the child; and
-- src:695 | (c) the person was also receiving any of the things mentioned in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (iv) on the day the child was born;
-- src:696 | then subsection (1) does not apply to the person for the purposes of that claim to the extent it relates to that flexible PPL day.
@ref s 31A(6A) (src:688-696)
GIVEN `the person has made an effective claim for parental leave pay for the flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day before the flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day before the flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day before the flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving parental leave pay for the child on the day before the flexible PPL day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving parental leave pay for the child on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31A(1) does not apply under subsection 31A(6A) for a flexible PPL day` MEANS
    JUST (        `the person has made an effective claim for parental leave pay for the flexible PPL day`
          AND (   `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day before the flexible PPL day`
               OR `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day before the flexible PPL day`
               OR `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day before the flexible PPL day`
               OR `the person was receiving parental leave pay for the child on the day before the flexible PPL day`)
          AND (   `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day the child was born`
               OR `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day the child was born`
               OR `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day the child was born`
               OR `the person was receiving parental leave pay for the child on the day the child was born`))

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next week day after a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a day is a week day` (day PLUS 1) THEN day PLUS 1
           IF `a day is a week day` (day PLUS 2) THEN day PLUS 2
           OTHERWISE day PLUS 3

GIVEN first IS A DATE, born IS A DATE, rest IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every day claimed is a flexible PPL day that is a week day and follows the one before` MEANS
    CONSIDER rest
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `a day is a week day` first AND `a day is a flexible PPL day for a child born on` first born EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WHEN second FOLLOWED BY others
        THEN `a day is a week day` first
             AND (`a day is a flexible PPL day for a child born on` first born EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             AND second EQUALS `the next week day after a day` first
             AND `every day claimed is a flexible PPL day that is a week day and follows the one before` second born others

-- src:697 | (6B) If:
-- src:698 | (b) a person has made an effective claim for parental leave pay for a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days for a child; and
-- src:699 | (c) that period consists only of consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that are week days; and
-- src:700 | (d) the person was receiving any of the following on the day before the start of that period:
-- src:701 | (i) a social security pension;
-- src:702 | (ii) a social security benefit;
-- src:703 | (iii) farm household allowance; and
-- src:704 | (e) the person was also receiving any of the things mentioned in subparagraphs (d)(i) to (iii) on the day the child was born;
-- src:705 | then subsection (1) does not apply to the person for the purposes of that claim to the extent that it relates to the period referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection.
@ref s 31A(6B) (src:697-705)
GIVEN `the claim is for a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that period consists only of consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that are week days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day before the start of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day before the start of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day before the start of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day the child was born` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31A(1) does not apply under subsection 31A(6B) to a period` MEANS
    JUST (        `the claim is for a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days`
          AND `that period consists only of consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that are week days`
          AND (   `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day before the start of that period`
               OR `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day before the start of that period`
               OR `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day before the start of that period`)
          AND (   `the person was receiving a social security pension on the day the child was born`
               OR `the person was receiving a social security benefit on the day the child was born`
               OR `the person was receiving farm household allowance on the day the child was born`))

-- src:706 | (7) Subsection 31AB(8) does not apply to a person in respect of a day in the newly arrived resident’s waiting period for the person if on that day the person holds, or is the former holder of, a visa in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of subsection 739A(6) of the Social Security Act.
@ref s 31A(7) (src:706-706)
GIVEN `on the day the person holds, or is the former holder of, a visa in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of subsection 739A(6) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(8) does not apply under subsection 31A(7) to a day` MEANS
    JUST `on the day the person holds, or is the former holder of, a visa in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of subsection 739A(6) of the Social Security Act`

-- src:707 | (7A) Subsection 31AB(8) does not apply to a person in respect of a day (the assessment day) in the newly arrived resident’s waiting period for the person if:
-- src:708 | (a) on the assessment day the person is a refugee or a former refugee; or
-- src:709 | (b) the following apply:
-- src:710 | (i) the person was a family member of another person at the time the other person became a refugee before the assessment day;
-- src:711 | (ii) the person is a family member of that other person on the assessment day or, if that other person has died, the person was a family member of that other person immediately before that other person died; or
-- src:712 | (c) the person is an Australian citizen on the assessment day; or
-- src:713 | (d) the person is residing in Australia on the assessment day and has held a special category visa on any day before the assessment day.
@ref s 31A(7A) (src:707-713)
GIVEN `on the assessment day the person is a refugee or a former refugee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a family member of another person at the time the other person became a refugee before the assessment day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a family member of that other person on the assessment day or, if that other person has died, was one immediately before that other person died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an Australian citizen on the assessment day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is residing in Australia on the assessment day and has held a special category visa on any day before the assessment day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 31AB(8) does not apply under subsection 31A(7A) to a day` MEANS
    JUST (        `on the assessment day the person is a refugee or a former refugee`
          OR (`the person was a family member of another person at the time the other person became a refugee before the assessment day` AND `the person is a family member of that other person on the assessment day or, if that other person has died, was one immediately before that other person died`)
          OR `the person is an Australian citizen on the assessment day`
          OR `the person is residing in Australia on the assessment day and has held a special category visa on any day before the assessment day`)

DECLARE `A term in subsection 31A(7A)` IS ONE OF
    `family member`
    `former refugee`
    refugee

-- src:714 | (8) For the purposes of subsection (7A):
-- src:715 | (a) family member has the meaning given by subsection 7(6D) of the Social Security Act; and
-- src:716 | (b) former refugee has the meaning given by subsection 7(1) of the Social Security Act; and
-- src:717 | (c) refugee has the meaning given by subsection 7(6B) of the Social Security Act.
@ref s 31A(8) (src:714-717)
GIVEN term IS A `A term in subsection 31A(7A)`
GIVETH A STRING
`the provision of the Social Security Act that gives the meaning of a term in subsection 31A(7A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `family member` THEN "subsection 7(6D) of the Social Security Act"
    WHEN `former refugee` THEN "subsection 7(1) of the Social Security Act"
    WHEN refugee THEN "subsection 7(6B) of the Social Security Act"
